 RevTeX. Substantial changes made"}], "first_author": {"emails": ["bassi@ictp.trieste.it"], "affiliations_identifiers": [{"schema": "ROR", "value": "https://ror.org/009gyvm78"}, {"schema": "ROR", "value": "https://ror.org/05j3snm48"}], "full_name": "Bassi, Angelo", "last_name": "Bassi", "first_name": "Angelo", "recid": 1258732}, "control_number": 654362, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.94.030401"}, {"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.94.030401"}], "earliest_date": "2004-06", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Bassi:2004eu"], "abstracts": [{"value": "We analyze the recently proposed mirror superposition experiment of Marshall, Simon, Penrose, and Bouwmeester, assuming that the mirror's dynamics contains a non-unitary term of the Lindblad type proportional to -[q,[q,\\rho]], with q the position operator for the center of mass of the mirror, and \\rho the statistical operator. We derive an exact formula for the fringe visibility for this system. We discuss the consequences of our result for tests of environmental decoherence and of collapse models. In particular, we find that with the conventional parameters for the CSL model of state vector collapse, maintenance of coherence is expected to within an accuracy of at least 1 part in 10^{8}. Increasing the apparatus coupling to environmental decoherence may lead to observable modifications of the fringe visibility, with time dependence given by our exact result."}, {"source": "arXiv", "value": "We analyze the recently proposed mirror superposition experiment of Marshall, Simon, Penrose, and Bouwmeester, assuming that the mirror's dynamics contains a non-unitary term of the Lindblad type proportional to -[q,[q,ρ]], with q the position operator for the center of mass of the mirror, and ρthe statistical operator. We derive an exact formula for the fringe visibility for this system. We discuss the consequences of our result for tests of environmental decoherence and of collapse models. In particular, we find that with the conventional parameters for the CSL model of state vector collapse, maintenance of coherence is expected to within an accuracy of at least 1 part in 10^8. Increasing the apparatus coupling to environmental decoherence may lead to observable modifications of the fringe visibility, with time dependence given by our exact result.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "refereed": true, "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "ADS", "value": "2005PhRvL..94c0401B"}, {"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-5928192"}, {"schema": "MSNET", "value": "2133521"}], "titles": [{"title": "Towards quantum superpositions of a mirror: Stochastic collapse analysis"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "Towards Quantum Superpositions of a Mirror: Stochastic Collapse Analysis"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "Towards Quantum Superpositions of a Mirror: an Exact Open Systems Analysis"}], "facet_author_name": ["2261527_Emiliano Ippoliti", "1018932_Stephen L. Adler", "1258732_Angelo Bassi"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:654362", "updated": "2026-02-06T10:02:03.983686"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.Lett.", "Phys. Rev. Lett."], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph", "hep-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/0406108"}]}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.94.030401&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.94.030401&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.94.030401&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.94.030401&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.94.030401&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "http